{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 43, :comments ["<b>For in sukkot I caused the children of Israel to dwell</b> — clouds of glory. This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 23:43), and it is the correct interpretation in my eyes according to the plain sense, for He commanded that the generations should know all the great deeds of YHWH that He did with them in wondrous fashion, that He caused them to dwell in clouds of His glory like a sukkah, as it is said: \"And YHWH will create over every dwelling place of Mount Zion and over its assemblies a cloud by day and smoke and the glow of flaming fire by night, for over all the glory there shall be a canopy (חֻפָּה) and a sukkah, for a shade by day from the heat\" and so forth (Isaiah 4:5–6). And since He had already explained that the cloud of YHWH was over them by day and the pillar of fire by night, He stated simply: \"for in sukkot I caused them to dwell\" — that I made for them clouds of My glory as sukkot to shield them. Now behold, He commanded at the beginning of the summer season, in remembrance of the exodus from Egypt in its month and at its appointed time, and He commanded at the beginning of the rainy season in remembrance of the continuous miracle that was performed for them all the days of their sojourn in the wilderness. And according to the opinion of the one who says they were actual sukkot (Sukkah 11a), they began to make them at the beginning of winter because of the cold, as is the custom of camps, and therefore He commanded concerning them at this season. And the remembrance — that they should know and remember that they were in the wilderness, that they did not enter a house and found no settled city for forty years, and HaShem was with them; they lacked nothing."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:58:56.283267627Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}